Good progress — this is now a different issue than the earlier patch-name mismatch.

The current failure is strictly from `system/fvSchemes` missing one required divergence entry for `pimpleFoam`:

- Error says: `keyword div((nuEff*dev2(T(grad(U))))) is undefined`
- So in `divSchemes`, you must **define exactly this keyword** (literal string), e.g.:

```foam
divSchemes
{
    default                             none;
    div(phi,U)                          Gauss linearUpwind grad(U);
    div((nuEff*dev2(T(grad(U)))))       Gauss linear;
}
```

Why this works:
- `pimpleFoam` momentum equation needs a discretization for the viscous stress divergence term.
- You already defined `div(phi,U)`, but not the viscous term entry, so it aborts at startup.

